---
// src/pages/security.astro
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Security & Responsibility | Solya Solana Validator"
  description="How Solya Solana Validator handles infrastructure security, key management, and staking safety. Independent validator running since 2021 in São Paulo, Brazil."
>
  <div class="security-page">
    <div class="container">

      <div class="security-header">
        <a href="/" class="security-back">← Back</a>
        <div class="security-label-wrap">
        <span class="section-label">solya.studio/security</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="security-title">Security &amp; Responsibility</h1>
        <p class="security-intro">
          Running a Solana validator since 2021 means security isn't a checklist —
          it's part of daily operations. Here's how Solya is managed and what
          that means for stakers.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="security-sections">

        <div class="security-section">
          <h2 class="security-section-title">Your funds are safe by design</h2>
          <div class="security-content">
            <p>
              Staking on Solana is non-custodial. Solya — like any validator on
              the network — has no access to your wallet or staked SOL. The
              Solana protocol handles reward distribution automatically at the
              end of each epoch. You can unstake at any time; funds become
              available once the current epoch closes, typically within 2–3 days.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="security-section">
          <h2 class="security-section-title">Infrastructure</h2>
          <div class="security-content">
            <p>
              The node runs on dedicated hardware in São Paulo, Brazil (Vultr/Edgevana,
              AS20473) — a deliberate location choice for Solana's geographic
              decentralization. The server is hardened, access is restricted to
              key-based authentication, and the validator client follows Anza and
              Solana Foundation release guidance.
            </p>
            <p>
              The node is connected to DoubleZero for filtered, low-latency
              validator communication, and runs the Jito BAM client for
              verifiable, tamper-resistant transaction scheduling.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="security-section">
          <h2 class="security-section-title">Key management</h2>
          <div class="security-content">
            <p>
              Identity key, vote key, and withdraw authority are fully separated.
              The withdraw authority is stored offline and never touches the
              validator server. Commission is set to 0% and there are no plans to
              change that. If it ever did change, it would be announced publicly
              well in advance.
            </p>
            <div class="security-keys">
              <div class="security-key-row">
                <span class="security-key-label">Identity</span>
                <code class="security-key-value">HwN6eoEe9N3kwHi66hpQDBMFPk6ASQGthWKPX5MZmisp</code>
              </div>
              <div class="security-key-row">
                <span class="security-key-label">Vote account</span>
                <code class="security-key-value">HwcVgFSgmfeeF7zGFUBLoVA8Hpx8rtwyfCrJ1npBaSVC</code>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="security-section">
          <h2 class="security-section-title">Safe staking practices</h2>
          <div class="security-content">
            <p>
              Keep your seed phrase offline and never share it. Use a trusted
              wallet —
              <a href="https://phantom.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Phantom</a>
              or
              <a href="https://solflare.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Solflare</a>
              both support native Solana staking. Stake through your wallet's
              staking interface or the options on the
              <a href="/#stake">Stake</a> page — never send SOL directly to
              any address.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .security-page {
    padding-top: calc(64px + 3rem);
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
    min-height: 100vh;
  }

  .security-header {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
  }

  .security-back {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }
  .security-back:hover {
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
    opacity: 1;
  }

  .security-title {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
  }

  .security-intro {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 600px;
  }

  .security-sections {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
    max-width: 820px;
  }

  .security-section {
    padding: 2rem 2.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .security-section:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .security-section-title {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    margin-bottom: 0.875rem;
  }

  .security-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.875rem;
  }

  .security-content p {
    font-size: 0.925rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .security-keys {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .security-key-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .security-key-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    min-width: 90px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .security-key-value {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 0.3rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    word-break: break-all;
  }

  .security-label-wrap {
  margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .security-section {
      padding: 1.5rem;
    }
    .security-key-label {
      min-width: 80px;
    }
  }
</style>